e \"unit_id_remap\" top-level: {\"U1_跨癌种关联图谱\":[\"U1_跨癌种关联图谱\"], \"U2_外部干扰与宿主背景\":[\"U2_外部干扰与宿主背景\"]}. The instruction says return unit_id_remap with new_unit_id -> old_unit_id. If unchanged, still provide.\n\nNeed chapter_updates: [{chapter_id:\"Ch1\", updated_plan:{...}}].\n\nNeed status:\"updated\".\n\nLet's craft U1 paragraph briefs in detail.\n\nU1 paragraph 1: point \"共性信号：高多样性与产 SCFA/免疫调节菌在多个队列中与较好结局相关，但属于观察性关联\".\ndevelopment: In NSCLC and melanoma systematic review/meta-analysis, high alpha diversity and Akkermansia/Faecalibacterium associated with better survival/response (P0298). Melanoma systematic review: SCFA-producing taxa positive, fungal dysbiosis worse (P0565). Pan-cancer multi-kingdom: high diversity/stable co-occurrence network C2 subtype associated with response (P0393). Mention these are observational, not causal.\nfinding_conditions: \"在 NSCLC 与黑色素瘤队列的系统综述/荟萃分析中，高α多样性及 Akkermansia、Faecalibacterium 等菌属与更好 ICI 结局相关（P0298）；黑色素瘤综述中 SCFA 产生菌富集与较好反应相关，真菌失调与较差预后相关（P0565）；跨癌种多界宏基因组分析中，高多样性与特定属组合/网络亚型与反应相关（P0393）。这些关联未证明因果。\"\nsource_handles [\"P0298\",\"P0565\",\"P0393\"]. Could also P0096/P0146 but maybe not needed. But original supporting includes them; can keep in supporting_studies.\n\nParagraph 2: point \"反转与阴性结果：同一菌属在不同癌种/人群/治疗史中方向不同；α多样性并非总有效\".\ndevelopment: mCRPC post-enzalutamide pembrolizumab: A. muciniphila lower in responders, S. salivarius in feces positive, oral sample no association; integrated index failed (P0270). Polish melanoma: responders higher P. copri/B. uniformis, nonresponders F. prausnitzii; diet high plant low dairy associated (P0545). SCRUM-Japan advanced solid tumors: alpha diversity not associated with ICI efficacy; high oral bacterial proportion associated with worse PFS, especially with PPI (P0289). HCC: bacteria/metabolites differ DCB vs NDB, fungi less (P0204). This shows cancer/population/treatment-history specificity.\nfinding_conditions: include n=23 mCRPC, 16S/qPCR, post-enzalutamide; Polish n=64 patients 16S/some metagenomics; SCRUM-Japan cohort 2 n=333 ICI, 16S, oral bacteria definition; HCC n=80, metagenomics/ITS2/metabolomics. Need not too detailed but enough.\nsource_handles [\"P0270\",\"P0545\",\"P0289\",\"P0204\"].\n\nParagraph 3: point \"跨队列统计：队列效应主导，无单一通用物种标志物\".\ndevelopment: P0478 integrated 5 new melanoma cohorts n=165 + 4 public n=147; PERMANOVA cohort explains variance ~10x clinical variables; leave-one-cohort-out AUC 0.59-0.60; only 31.4% cross tests >0.6; meta identifies panel B. pseudocatenulatum, Roseburia, A. muciniphila but no single consistent; CRC control shows strong consistent biomarker using same methods, so not purely methodological. P0170 enterotype-specific markers (Collinsella E2, Bacteroides E1) show community context. Conditions: advanced cutaneous melanoma; observational; residual confounding; strain-level unresolved.\nsource_handles [\"P0478\",\"P0170\"].\n\nParagraph 4: point \"治疗方案与分辨率边界：微生物预测签名依赖方案与菌株/基因特征\".\ndevelopment: JCOG2007 ancillary phase III NSCLC: baseline 16S from 270? (295 enrolled, 270 samples) comparing NIC dual checkpoint + chemo vs PC PD-1 + chemo; Fusicatenibacter/Butyricicoccus high in NIC associated with better OS (HR 0.56/0.52), Prevotellaceae NK3B31 high with higher death risk (HR 2.33); low abundance/alpha diversity linked severe AEs? Need careful: safety maybe not central. Then P0015: strain-level signature in CICB rare tumors AUC 0.73; external CICB AUC 0.65 but anti-PD-1 monotherapy AUC 0.51; indicates regimen-specific not tumor-universal. P0437 gene-level with biological priors outperforms taxonomy in CICB but limited by regimen. Could include P0437. But paragraph might be too long. Use P0585, P0015, P0437 maybe.\nfinding_conditions: \"JCOG2007 为晚期 NSCLC III 期试验附属生物标志物研究，基线粪便 16S，比较 NIC 与 PC；HR 来自该研究的亚组关联，不能外推为所有 NSCLC 或所有 ICI 方案。CA209-538 为 CICB 罕见实体瘤队列，外部验证限于 CICB 与抗 PD-1 单药比较，AUC 约 0.65 与 0.51。\"\nsource_handles [\"P0585\",\"P0015\",\"P0437\"].\n\nU1 supporting_studies: Need list with contribution and paper_i