y but functional convergence (SCFA, DC activation etc); P0511 meta melanoma vitamin B metabolism enriched; P0437 gene-level signatures? Maybe P0437 more predictive, but can mention gene-level with biological priors. Use P0364,P0511,P0437.\nBut P0364 is bibliometric and mechanistic synthesis, not original data; okay as synthesis. P0511 is meta-analysis of melanoma MGS, vitamin B metabolism. P0437 is gene-level model, CICB. Good.\nParagraph 3: reversals/negative.\nParagraph 4: cross-cohort heterogeneity.\nParagraph 5: regimen-specific.\n\nNeed maybe not include P0096/P0146? They are reviews; can support paragraph 1 as background. Include in supporting_studies but not paragraph source? Could add to paragraph 1 source_handles: P0096,P0146. But too many; okay.\n\nNeed check P0096: NSCLC review from biomarker to therapeutic strategy. It may list Akkermansia etc. P0146: gut microbiota shapes cancer immunotherapy responses. Good.\n\nU1 supporting_studies contributions must be accurate. Let's draft:\n- P0298: systematic review/meta-analysis NSCLC/melanoma; high diversity, Akkermansia/Faecalibacterium positive; antibiotic negative; observational moderate certainty.\n- P0565: systematic review melanoma; SCFA producers positive, fungal dysbiosis negative; heterogeneity prevents quantitative meta.\n- P0393: multi-kingdom pan-cancer; high diversity and genus combinations predict efficacy; observational, mixed cancers.\n- P0364: bibliometric/mechanistic synthesis; functional convergence amid taxonomic variability; not quantitative.\n- P0511: melanoma meta-analysis; Faecalibacterium and vitamin B metabolism; limited external AUC and no multiple correction.\n- P0437: gene-level signatures with bio priors; better than taxonomy, regimen-dependent.\n- P0270: mCRPC; A. muciniphila negative, S. salivarius positive; small n, post-enzalutamide.\n- P0545: Polish melanoma; P. copri/B. uniformis positive, F. prausnitzii in nonresponders; diet; small, observational.\n- P0289: SCRUM-Japan; alph